{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/red-cup-engineering/guix-machine-release-service/pulls/149","id":4901064383,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVBRbUs8AAAABJCBOvw","html_url":"https://github.com/red-cup-engineering/guix-machine-release-service/pull/149","diff_url":"https://github.com/red-cup-engineering/guix-machine-release-service/pull/149.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/red-cup-engineering/guix-machine-release-service/pull/149.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/red-cup-engineering/guix-machine-release-service/issues/149","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/red-cup-engineering/guix-machine-release-service/pulls/149/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/red-cup-engineering/guix-machine-release-service/pulls/149/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/red-cup-engineering/guix-machine-release-service/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/red-cup-engineering/guix-machine-release-service/issues/149/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/red-cup-engineering/guix-machine-release-service/statuses/e840d63cfbdcff09eab07f68937ce0114efc4920","number":149,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Preserve unavailable measurements and admit registry consumer sources","user":{"login":"emsenn","id":111507,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTUwNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111507?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/emsenn","html_url":"https://github.com/emsenn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emsenn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emsenn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emsenn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emsenn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emsenn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emsenn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emsenn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emsenn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emsenn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The package runner previously classified unavailable test processes as failed assertions, and the retained native comparison required a root PNPM workspace that the current deployment inventory no longer owns. This change preserves unavailable measurements and introduces a closed, source-only registry admission arm in the existing receiver.\n\nThe v4 request binds independently selected inventory roots, exact target owners and mounted coordinates. The consumer's committed package exports must select that exact machine/channels definition. Admission binds manifest, native lock and local configuration presence/digests, retains requested heads and complete graph/target deltas, and verifies source custody again. It accepts no caller test command, package inventory, recipe or success receipt. Historical v2/v3 behavior remains distinct.\n\nThis arm always returns incomplete with runtimeAcceptance false. It does not implement the paired Code installation/runtime and LAGOON product/target executor. Local policy evidence is not a complete inherited-policy guarantee; receivingTests property presence is not valid enrollment; committed lock identity is not PNPM validation; graph membership is not product participation.\n\nCandidate: `e840d63cfbdcff09eab07f68937ce0114efc4920`, tree `e6043514bd6078091fbaebfb6e8772e610d07a5b`, following the parent specification commit `2e237884fa001505eec726e68a4550eab8c283ec`.\n\nValidation:\n\n- The three selected original owner suites plus four registry source cases pass 130/130, no skips. Fixtures now supply canonical origins and committed machine definitions, allowing their original later assertions to execute. One obsolete target-lock assertion migrated to independent exact channel blobs, while both target lock fields are explicitly required to remain null; root, delta and nested-definition assertions remain.\n- Independently extracted exact committed source archive: 130/130, no skips. Archive SHA256 `e94e7aef39c8f116f089422abc3b74eeb1d76f7d8fd5db7fc415ab2543627294`.\n- The candidate source reader successfully read real BCF consumer `561-group/bare-cedar-fog-services-section@9eecfafcb90be5ab4499ce607cae4949c5748e30`, tree `0fbf63a8c1d856d210ec585b195a31f05c1f7fe7`: manifest `e09b25cc348db6a3b5596d6cca69dd9884cbd18e`, lock `5988651ca8631380e04acd9b12348d54758e29b4`, workspace policy `9b54ef685668a440f61c6dc070518d6c0ef81859`, machine `44e6713eb5bcd486a743c275482198c4cb307440`. It retained absent receiving enrollment. This was a committed source reading, not installation or complete inventory-pair receiving.\n- Earlier unchanged native package comparison remains separately qualified by its 17/17 integration against the genuine packed/frozen-installed original Code provider in [Code PR2](https://github.com/red-cup-engineering/node-runtime-release-promotion-service/pull/2) at `b2350f299ea45a8e9a26bad2a119abe0fd880be6`. Provider source and exact packed-artifact controls passed 11/11 each. Those receipts do not establish current registry machine receiving.\n- Independent review receives this exact source-only increment and preserves its incomplete boundary.\n\nRemaining implementation: the actual paired fixed Code frozen-install/runtime and LAGOON build/check-target composition, complete policy custody, original and removed engineering obligations, requested-change participation, final source/store integrity and non-vacuous verdict. Current publication supplier `5a85a4f3ef6c2dc7c074d740633507b39b0a8057` stages local workspace policy; release exclusions and inherited effective policy remain distinct concerns. Its releases:[] route adds no release exemption. BCF authors age zero in its own manifest/configuration; this does not change FeltOS's separate 1,440-minute policy.\n\nThe pinned BCF consumer has no receivingTests enrollment. Genuine paired runtime/store/target receiving and the existing machine merge gate remain unfulfilled. Keep this PR draft. No merge, live installation, deployment or operating acceptance is claimed. Related: #101; LAGOON read-only target [PR13](https://github.com/red-cup-engineering/computer-deployment-engine/pull/13).","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-17T14:50:52Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T17:08:37Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"d4ca0e7a899f905a9e756cb735085f1267c6bb09","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"red-cup-engineering:codex/registry-native-comparison-contract-20261017","ref":"codex/registry-native-comparison-contract-20261017","repo":{"id":1410620242,"node_id":"R_kgDOVBRbUg","name":"guix-machine-release-service","full_name":"red-cup-engineering/guix-machine-release-service","owner":{"login":"red-cup-engineering","id":308933773,"node_id":"O_kgDOEmn0jQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/308933773?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-cup-engineering","html_url":"https://github.com/red-cup-engineering","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-cup-engineering/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-cup-engineering/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-cup-engineering/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-cup-engineering/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-cup-engineering/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-cup-engineering/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-cup-engineering/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-cup-engineering/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-cup-engineering/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_ad